\section{Matching with the band}{

Modal shaping uses squared relative error to Sa.mean and squared relative
violations below Sa.low or above Sa.high, together with the modal-factor
movement penalty. During record scaling, shape.bandWeight weights individual
record band violations, while shape.deficitWeight weights the suite-mean
deficit below Sa.mean. Both stages use the target band including zero (PGA).
match/target.csv publishes Tn, Sa.low, Sa.mean and Sa.high in units.psa;
metadata/runMatch.json copies the contract, including target.envelope.
}

\section{Target envelope}{

target.envelope is a required JSON object with lower and upper fields,
for example \code{\{"lower": "0.50", "upper": "0.95"\}}.
Each bound and target.p select an exact p label in the target table:
\code{"mean"} or a decimal of the form \code{0.<digits>} strictly between
0 and 1, such as \code{"0.50"}. Percentages (\code{"50"}, \code{"50\%"})
and p prefixes (\code{"p50"}) are rejected.
Numeric scalars are converted to text and must satisfy the same decimal
format and literal table match; \code{"0.5"} and \code{"0.50"} are different labels.
The lower, central and upper labels must be distinct; duplicate object keys
and target.envelope.ID are rejected. \code{"mean"} is valid for either bound
or target.p when its rows exist and satisfy the band checks.
lower, target.p and upper become Sa.low, Sa.mean and Sa.high respectively;
Sa.mean denotes the selected central curve even when target.p is a quantile.
The curves require identical Tn meshes containing zero (PGA) and positive
periods, with finite ordinates satisfying \code{0 < Sa.low <= Sa.mean <= Sa.high}
at every retained period. Tn is in seconds.
Ordinates are read in target.units (default g) and converted to units.psa;
conversions between g and mm/s2 (or mm/s^2) are supported, and identical
units are retained.
